{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>במי</b> Five times in the Masorah: במי הנדה. אך במי נדה יתחטא. במי מריבת קדש. במי הירדן. אם התרחצתי במי שלג. This is what they expounded: \"And Elazar the priest said to the men of the army\" — since Moshe came to a state of anger, he came to a state of error, for he forgot to instruct them the laws of גיעול. This is במי מריבת — since he came to a state of מריבה, he erred במי נדה. במי הירדן — to teach that the waters of the Jordan are like מי נדה and require forty se'ah. And this is like Shmuel, who forbids (Shabbat 65) immersing in rivers, lest the dripping waters multiply upon the flowing waters and they do not purify by way of זחילה. במי שלג — to teach that one may make a mikveh from snow, as stated in chapter 7 of Massekhet Mikva'ot: The men of Meidba testified about Rabbi Yishma'el that he would say to them: Go and bring snow and make a mikveh at the outset."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "The opening ה במסרה appears to mean 'five in the Masorah' (ה = 5); the five listed phrases match the count. Translated hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:37.039897642Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}